        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2000 Solheim Cup\n- Places: Loch Lomond Golf Club, Luss, Dunbartonshire, Scotland, Rossdhu Mansion\n- Organizations: Clan Colquhoun\n- People: Dale Reid\n- Roles: Europe player, Europe non-playing captain\n\nFacts:\n- Dale Reid played for Europe in the first four Solheim Cups in 1990, 1992, 1994, and 1996.\n- The 6th Solheim Cup Match was held between 6 and 8 October 2000 at Loch Lomond Golf Club in Luss, Dunbartonshire, Scotland.\n- Dale Reid was Europe's non-playing captain in 2000 and 2002.\n- Loch Lomond Golf Club occupies land previously held by Clan Colquhoun.\n- Loch Lomond Golf Club uses Rossdhu Mansion, the seat of Clan Colquhoun, as its clubhouse.",
